    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on aggressive baserunning and high-leverage platoon matchups. Our top play is undoubtedly **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12), whose profile is maximized by a favorable matchup against Lowder. The combination of an elite 100% stolen base opportunity against a slow delivery and the prime leadoff spot gives him our highest efficiency score of the day. Similarly, **Lars Nootbaar** (67.11) represents a high-upside play; the wind blowing out adds a crucial boost to his projection, and his dynamic platoon advantage against Tidwell solidifies his spot in the lineup. **Yordan Alvarez** (66.16) remains a set-and-forget asset, as his elite xwOBA effectively mitigates the lack of a traditional platoon edge, while **Junior Caminero** (64.76) rounds out the high-efficiency core by capitalizing on the protection of the #3 hole against Mize.\n\nThe benching process was tight today, with **Carson Benge** (55.59) falling just short of the starting cut. While **Carson Benge** posted a competitive score thanks to a favorable park and solid platoon split, the current depth of our outfield and utility slots\u2014specifically the higher ceiling of **Junior Caminero** and the speed profiles of our starting five\u2014pushed him to the pine. We are monitoring the status of **Kyle Schwarber** and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, both of whom are currently listed as \"Lineup Pending.\" Should the official lineups force a shuffle, we are prepared to pivot to the bench, though the lack of an elite replacement for their specific power-output profiles makes them high-priority starts if confirmed. Conversely, **Dillon Dingler** faces a difficult task against Skubal; his score of 48.39 is buoyed by his platoon advantage and expected order placement, but the elite SP skill of the opposing pitcher makes this a matchup we will watch closely for early-game volatility.",
